---
import Layout from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout
  title="Research hub"
  description="Bibliography, evidence labels, and reading library for zhao-langxi HRI essays."
  canonical="https://zhao-langxi.github.io/zhao-langxi/research.html"
  current="research"
>
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <header>
      <p>Research and methods</p>
      <h1>Research hub</h1>
      <p>Each file below supports the essays. Open the one that matches what you need: reading lists, citation rules, or draft review notes.</p>
    </header>
    <article>
      <ul class="resource-list">
        <li>
          <h2><a href={`${base}research/evidence-labels.md`}>Evidence labels</a></h2>
          <p>Read this first if you are new. It defines <strong>Observed</strong>, <strong>Reported</strong>, <strong>Interpreted</strong>, and <strong>Open question</strong> on every essay.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h2><a href={`${base}research/bibliography.md`}>Open bibliography</a></h2>
          <p>Cited and candidate sources with stable links. Use when you want to check a claim or suggest a reference via GitHub.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h2><a href={`${base}research/reading-library.md`}>HRI reading library</a></h2>
          <p>Papers, tools, and open robotics projects grouped for essay research ... not a course syllabus.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h2><a href={`${base}editorial/essay-reviews.md`}>Essay reviews</a></h2>
          <p>Editorial notes on existing drafts (argument, repetition, HRI bridge). No silent overwrites of essay HTML.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h2><a href={`${base}editorial/flagship-plan.md`}>Flagship essay plan</a></h2>
          <p>Working outline for <em>The right to interrupt</em> ... interruption, accessibility, and authority in shared spaces.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h2><a href={`${base}research/notes/README.md`}>Research notes folder</a></h2>
          <p>Scratch notes and reading logs that may feed future essays. Informal; not published as finished work.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Contributing references</h2>
      <p>
        Use GitHub Issues (template: research reference) or a pull request that adds a row to <code>bibliography.md</code> with a stable link.
        Do not paste paywalled full text without permission.
      </p>
      <p><a href={base}>← Home</a></p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
